From: mscharged-port
Subject: Type, delete and paste the friend code with the keyboard
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native desktop convenience; the keypad behaves as before.

SHOnlineFriendCodeEntry enters a friend code with an on-screen keypad that
the Wii Remote's pointer presses. Natively the keyboard presses it too: every
frame the screen takes input, Update asks the host for the next key
(MSChargedTakeFriendCodeKey, src/platform/friend_code_keys.cpp). The number
keys of the top row and the numeric keypad press its digits and Backspace its
delete button, through OnKeypadPointerPress for the pointer's player, so a
key fills or empties the selected box with the keypad's sound, as a press of
its button does. Delete empties the whole code (ClearDigitTexts, the first
box selected, the delete button's sound), and a code pasted with Ctrl+V,
Cmd+V or Shift+Insert (12 digits; spaces, dashes and dots allowed) types
itself in, a key a frame; a paste that is no code gets the keypad's error
sound. While the screen takes no input (its transitions, a save, a popup) it
does not ask, and the host drops keys once it has not asked for a quarter of
a second. While it asks, Backspace, Delete and a paste stay out of the game,
so Backspace is not Back there; Escape still is, and Enter A. Console builds
are unchanged.

